  "sourceQuote": "$\\angle BCD = 90^\\circ$, $\\angle DBC = 45^\\circ$이므로 $\\triangle BCD$는 직각이등변삼각형이고 $\\overline{CD} = \\overline{BC} = 10\\text{ cm}$이다. $\\triangle ABC$에서 $\\angle C = 90^\\circ$, $\\angle A = 30^\\circ$이므로 $$\\tan 30^\\circ = \\dfrac{\\overline{BC}}{\\overline{CA}} \\implies \\overline{CA} = \\dfrac{10}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}} = 10\\sqrt{3}\\text{ (cm)}$$ 따라서 $$\\overline{AD} = \\overline{CA} - \\overline{CD} = (10\\sqrt{3} - 10)\\text{ cm}$$"
